            <div xml:id="d529">

                <pb facs="0682" n="583" sameAs="frus:frus1936v02/pg583"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">800.51W89 France/1058: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of
                            State to the Ambassador in France</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Bullitt</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1936-11-30T19:00:00-05:00">November 30, 1936—7
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>487, Your 1160, November 28, 1 p.m. I entirely approve of your restrained
                    response to matters brought up in your interview as reported in the telegram
                    referred to above and in my opinion these matters should be allowed to remain in
                    abeyance until the President has returned to Washington.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Moore</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
